{"duration_api_ms":8385,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"31804c75-4e4f-43d3-86c5-6b0d108cec75","total_cost_usd":0.0010278,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":670,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1521,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1175},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":670,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1521,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":670,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":670},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1213,"outputTokens":1545,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":670,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0010278,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1175,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":670,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Auditor selection:** Under Section 32(a) of the Investment Company Act of 1940, the trust's board of trustees selects the independent registered public accounting firm. The selection must be approved by a majority of the trustees who are not \"interested persons.\" In practice, the audit committee, which is composed of independent trustees, recommends the auditor, and the full board votes on it, usually at an in-person meeting.\n\n**When shareholder ratification can be omitted:** Shareholder ratification is not a general statutory requirement for auditor selection. It is typically sought only at a shareholder meeting, such as an annual meeting. A multi-series trust can omit ratification when it is not holding an annual shareholder meeting, which generally occurs when state law and the trust's governing documents do not require one and the trust relies on the applicable exemptions from annual meeting requirements. The Statement of Additional Information and any proxy materials will disclose whether ratification is sought.\n\nConfirm the specifics against the trust's governing documents and current SEC rules, since I may not reflect the latest guidance.","ttft_ms":6241,"type":"result","duration_ms":7900,"uuid":"09de6b86-2476-4d3b-96ca-88c9137bca27","ttft_stream_ms":720,"time_to_request_ms":66,"first_content_frame_ms":720,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
